---
// Blinds, shutters and ceiling fans — the last of the six "Appliances" leaf
// pages under the Home Cleaning mega-menu. See carpet-and-rug-cleaning.astro
// for the shared reasoning behind this group, and
// src/data/appliance-services.ts for the cluster links.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS. All copy is DRAFTED from the brand foundation
// document. Facts only TLB holds ship as visible [brackets].
//
// WHAT THIS PAGE IS ACTUALLY SELLING. Nobody wakes up wanting their blinds
// cleaned. This is the least urgent service in the group and the copy accepts
// that rather than manufacturing urgency: it sells the job as the one a
// regular clean never has time for, best done as an add-on. The strongest
// honest hooks are the ones the page uses — a ceiling fan turned on after
// months off, and the fact that this is above eye level so it is invisible
// until sunlight hits it.
//
// ⚠️ NO HEALTH CLAIM. Dust is the other obvious angle and it leads straight
// to allergens and air quality, which is exactly where this site does not go.
// Same rule as the mattress and mould pages, same reason (BFD 5.3). Say the
// blinds are dusty and leave it there.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - ULTRASONIC vs IN SITU. Venetian and fabric blinds are cleaned either in
//     place, or taken down and put through an ultrasonic bath off site. They
//     are completely different services: different price, and one of them
//     means the customer has bare windows for a day or two. Confirm which TLB
//     does. §4 currently describes in-situ cleaning, which is the more common
//     answer for a domestic cleaner, and branded FAQ 4 hedges the other.
//   - HEIGHT AND SAFETY. Ceiling fans and tall windows mean working at
//     height off a ladder. Confirm TLB's own limit — how high the team will
//     go, and where a two-storey void or a raked ceiling becomes a job they
//     decline. The page currently says there is a limit without naming it.
//   - ROLLER AND FABRIC BLINDS. Confirm whether TLB cleans fabric and roller
//     blinds at all, or only hard surfaces (venetians, shutters, verticals).
//     Water marks fabric blinds permanently and plenty of cleaners decline.
//   - Pricing basis bracketed.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: hero is a family B cut-out keyed against green (white blind
// slats cannot be keyed off white). See
// src/assets/home_cleaning/appliances/IMAGE-PROMPTS.md.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
